---
import "../styles/automorphic.css";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="How Automorphic handles account information." />
    <title>Privacy — Automorphic</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header><a class="brand" href="/"><img src="/automorphic-mark.svg" width="34" height="34" alt="" />Automorphic</a></header>
    <main style="max-width:760px;margin:80px auto;padding:0 24px 80px;line-height:1.8">
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(36px,6vw,64px);margin-bottom:32px">Your account and privacy.</h1>
      <p>Updated September 12, 2026.</p>
      <h2>Information used to sign in</h2>
      <p>Automorphic stores your name, verified email address, account identifier, and profile photo when supplied by Google. We use this information to create your account and recognize you when you return. Authentication records also include sessions and may include your IP address and browser information.</p>
      <h2>Services that process this information</h2>
      <p>Google verifies your identity when you choose Google sign-in. Convex hosts account and authentication records. Resend delivers verification codes when you choose email sign-in. These services process information needed to provide those features.</p>
      <h2>Your trading workspace</h2>
      <p>Signing in does not upload your local workspace files. When you use an AI provider or connect a broker, information required for that feature is sent to the service you use. Your provider and broker have their own privacy policies.</p>
      <h2>Sessions and account controls</h2>
      <p>Automorphic uses browser storage or desktop credential storage to keep you signed in. You can sign out from your profile menu. Signing out ends the session; it does not delete your account.</p>
      <h2>Questions and deletion requests</h2>
      <p>To ask about your account information, request a correction, or request account deletion, contact <a href="mailto:munachi@ekogenie.com">munachi@ekogenie.com</a>.</p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
